.TH MU2EDAQ\-SETUP\-ENV 1 "2026-07-23" "Mu2e DAQ" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq\-setup\-env \- activate a compatibility-test package's venv and build PATH in the current shell
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B source mu2edaq\-setup\-env.sh
.RI [ package " | " \-\-list ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mu2edaq\-setup\-env.sh
is a helper for working interactively with the venvs and CMake build
directories produced by
.BR mu2edaq\-build\-all.sh .
It must be
.B sourced,
not executed, because it modifies the calling shell's environment
.RB ( PATH ", " QT_QPA_PLATFORM ,
and venv activation state); running it as
.I ./mu2edaq\-setup\-env.sh
has no effect on the parent shell.
.PP
Given a package name, it activates that package's Python virtual
environment (if one exists under
.IR .compat/venvs/<package> )
and prepends any CMake build output directories for that package (if any
exist under
.IR .compat/build/<package> " or " .compat/build/<package>\-\-* )
to
.BR PATH ,
so built binaries and installed console scripts are runnable directly
by name.
.PP
Called with no argument, or with
.BR \-\-list ,
it does not modify the environment; it only prints what venvs and CMake
build directories are currently available.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I package
Name of a package under
.I .compat/venvs
and/or
.IR .compat/build ,
e.g.\&
.BR mu2edaq\-fts .
A trailing slash is stripped, so shell tab-completion on the directory
listing works unmodified.
.TP
.B \-\-list
List the venvs and CMake build directories currently present instead of
activating anything. This is also what happens when no argument is given.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_COMPAT_DIR
Root directory the script searches for venvs and build output. Default:
.IR <repo\-root>/.compat ,
matching
.BR mu2edaq\-build\-all.sh .
.PP
On successful activation the script exports:
.TP
.B PATH
Prefixed with the package's venv
.I bin/
directory (via the venv's own
.I activate
script) and, if present, its CMake build director(ies).
.TP
.B QT_QPA_PLATFORM
Left as-is if already set in the environment, otherwise exported empty so
Qt/GUI binaries launched from the shell pick the normal windowed platform
plugin (unlike the test harness, which forces
.BR offscreen ).
.SH EXAMPLES
See what has been built so far:
.EX
    source mu2edaq\-setup\-env.sh \-\-list
.EE
Activate a package's venv and PATH, then run its CLI directly:
.EX
    source mu2edaq\-setup\-env.sh mu2edaq\-fts
    python mu2edaq_fts.py \-\-help
.EE
Activate a CMake-built package and run the built binary by name:
.EX
    source mu2edaq\-setup\-env.sh mu2edaq\-trigger\-scalers
    mu2edaq\-trigger\-scalers \-\-help
.EE
.SH NOTES
Nothing happens (silently) if the named package has neither a venv nor a
build directory yet \(em run
.B mu2edaq\-build\-all.sh
for that package first.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq\-build\-all (1),
.BR mu2edaq\-test\-all (1)
